    // ID using the method +link{DataSource.get()}, regardless of whether it's actually bound
    // to the browser <code>window</code> object.
    // @visibility external
    //<

    //> @attr loadScreenSettings.omitDataSources (Array of Identifier : varies : IRW)
    // DataSource IDs in the screen to skip and not load when the screen is loaded.  It is
    // assumed that these IDs represent DataSources that are already globally-bound on the
    // client.
    // <P>
    // The special value of "*" can be specified for this property to indicate that <b>all</b>
    // DataSources should be omitted.
    // <P>
    // Note that, unless +link{omitLoadedDataSources} is false, all loaded DataSources will by
    // default be added to whatever value you provide (making that also the default for this
    // property).
    // @visibility external
    //<

    //> @attr loadScreenSettings.omitLoadedDataSources (boolean : true : IRW)
    // Whether to implicitly add all DataSources currently loaded on the client to
    // +link{omitDataSources} in +link{RPCManager.loadScreen()}.  Setting this false would only
    // make sense in connection with setting +link{clobberDataSources} true, and would create
    // more potential work for the server since many more DataSources could be output.
    // <P>
    // Note that here we consider the "loaded DataSources" to be those that are registered
    // with the DataSource module (i.e. available by ID via +link{DataSource.get()}),
    // regardless of whether they're actually bound to the browser <code>window</code> object.
