    //> @classMethod EditContext.createPaletteNodesFromJSON()
    // Creates palette nodes from JSON (either the JSON string or the decoded Object / Array of
    // Object that are the precursor nodes), replacing node references.
    // <p>
    // If <code>allowLegacyFormat</code> is <code>true</code>, then the precursor nodes may
    // be in the legacy format:
    // <pre>
    // {
    //   _constructor: "<type>",
    //   // .. instance defaults
    // }
    // </pre>
    // .. and if the nodes appear to be in that format, a reference to another node is a string
    // of the form "ref:&lt;ID&gt;".
    // <p>
    // If <code>allowLegacyFormat</code> is anything other than <code>true</code>, then
    // precursor nodes are in the new format. This is essentially a +link{PaletteNode}, except
    // that a reference to another <code>PaletteNode</code> may be made using a string of the
    // form "withID:&lt;ID&gt;".
    //
    // @param jsonString (String | Object | Array of Object) The JSON string or its decoding.
    // @param [allowLegacyFormat] (Boolean) <code>true</code> to allow the legacy precursor
    // node format to be used.
    // @param [keepGlobals] (Array of String) Array of node IDs to preserve in the returned
    // <code>PaletteNode</code>s. If <code>keepGlobals</code> is a one-element array with the
    // single value +link{RPC.ALL_GLOBALS}, then all node IDs are preserved. Otherwise, any
    // node ID that is not within <code>keepGlobals</code> is cleared.
